Ungate stop-color and stop-opacity in stylo's Servo build.

This targets the STYLO repository (https://github.com/servo/stylo), not
servo -- it sits outside the numbered servo series, like stylo-0001 and
stylo-0002.

Both properties are behind #[cfg(feature = "gecko")], so in Servo a
gradient stop has no colour and no opacity: neither the CSS form
(<stop style="stop-color:blue">) nor the presentation attribute
(<stop stop-color="blue">) parses, and every gradient comes out empty.
There is no Gecko-specific machinery behind either -- stop-color is a
plain Color and stop-opacity a plain Opacity -- so the gate looks like
an artefact of Gecko having been the only consumer.

Consumed by servo patch 0017, which reads them off the cascade so that
stylesheet-driven and currentColor stops work rather than only literal
attributes.

To try it: check out stylo at the rev pinned in servo's Cargo.lock,
apply, and add a [patch."https://github.com/servo/stylo"] section
redirecting all eleven stylo-repo crates at the local checkout.

diff --git a/style/properties/longhands.toml b/style/properties/longhands.toml
index 27d96b253..0d55e5e32 100644
--- a/style/properties/longhands.toml
+++ b/style/properties/longhands.toml
@@ -1955,7 +1955,6 @@ affects = "layout"
 type = "Color"
 initial = "computed::Color::BLACK"
 struct = "svg"
-engine = "gecko"
 spec = "https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/pservers.html#StopColorProperties"
 affects = "paint"
 
@@ -1963,7 +1962,6 @@ affects = "paint"
 type = "Opacity"
 initial = "1.0"
 struct = "svg"
-engine = "gecko"
 spec = "https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/pservers.html#StopOpacityProperty"
 affects = "paint"
 
